from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((R/'RESULTS.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));q=json.loads((R/'COMPUTATION-QUALIFICATION.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x))
def pct(x):return f'{100*x:.2f}%'
def table(h,rows):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(v)+'</th>' for v in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in r)+'</tr>' for r in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · ACTUAL-LAYOUT POWER AUDIT · v97</p><h1>How much could the transition test miss?</h1><p class="notice"><strong>'+e(d['status'])+'.</strong> All eight layout/view combinations fail both frozen detection benchmarks. The exact computation remains valid; its earlier implementation qualification did not establish sensitivity to these moderate actual-layout alternatives. No manuscript result was rescored.</p>'
body+='<p>Bath hand2/B/P and Starred hand3/B/P, H/F separate. This audit reuses every actual v96 conditional span distribution and the unchanged original opening-family ×28 correction. It does not substitute 128 identical toy spans for the observed mixture.</p>'
body+='<h2>Frozen full-coverage benchmarks</h2>'+table(['Section / hand','Reading','View','Variable spans','Power at weight1.5','80% gate','Power at weight2','90% gate','First frozen weight reaching80%'],[[e(x['section']+' / '+x['hand']),x['reading'],e(x['view']),x['variable_spans'],pct(x['benchmark_moderate_power']),'PASS' if x['moderate_gate'] else 'FAIL',pct(x['benchmark_strong_power']),'PASS' if x['strong_gate'] else 'FAIL',e(x['first_frozen_forward_ratio_with_80pct_power'])] for x in d['layouts']])
body+='<p>Benchmarks were frozen before calculating power: at least80% detection for a full-coverage forward weight1.5 and at least90% for weight2, separately in every panel/view. These are audit requirements, not thresholds retroactively imposed on the correctness of the v96 algorithm. Every failure remains.</p>'
body+='<h2>What the effect sizes mean</h2><p>D is the net number of sh X qok minus qok X sh. An alternative weights a compatible arrangement by r raised to its D score, with r fixed in advance. This favours higher residual ordering without changing any permitted word multiset, endpoint or adjacent class-transition count. A weight1.5 is <strong>not</strong> a prediction of50%more observed pairs.</p><p>Weights were1.10,1.25,1.5,2,3,4, with null1 and reciprocal reverse-direction controls. In the earlier two-path +/-1toy, the corresponding positive-path probability is r²/(1+r²). Each actual layout has a different mixture of score ranges; hundreds of variable spans are not interchangeable with identical toy choices.</p><p>Alternatives are view-specific mathematical models, not one shared synthetic manuscript evaluated through both views. H/F are not multiplied into an independent-replication power estimate.</p>'
body+='<h2>Expected score shifts and the fixed detection threshold</h2>'
rows=[]
for x in d['layouts']:
 for weight in ['3/2','2']:
  c=next(c for c in d['power_cases'] if c['original_panel_index']==x['original_panel_index'] and c['view']==x['view'] and c['coverage']=='1' and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']==weight)
  rows.append([e(x['section']),x['reading'],e(x['view']),weight,f'{x["null_mean"]:.2f}',x['critical_forward_min'],f'{c["alternative_mean"]:.2f}',f'{c["mean_shift_D"]:.2f}',f'{c["mean_shift_in_null_SD"]:.2f}',pct(c['correct_direction_power'])])
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','Weight','Null mean D','Smallest forward rejecting D','Alternative mean D','Mean shift D','Shift /nullSD','Detection power'],rows)
body+='<p>These shifts are consequences of the fixed alternatives, not fits to the observed manuscript score. The actual observed D and its p-value were not used as a target or retested.</p>'
body+='<h2>Localized effects are easier to miss</h2><p>Quarter/half coverage uses one preselected SHA256-ranked subset of variable spans in each layout/view. Selection uses locator/start position and null variability, never observed score or preferred direction. It is not an average or worst case over all affected subsets.</p>'
rows=[]
for x in d['layouts']:
 vals=[]
 for fraction in ['1','1/2','1/4']:
  c=next(c for c in d['power_cases'] if c['original_panel_index']==x['original_panel_index'] and c['view']==x['view'] and c['coverage']==fraction and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']=='2');vals.append(pct(c['correct_direction_power'])+' · '+str(c['selected_variable_spans'])+' affected spans')
 rows.append([e(x['section']),x['reading'],e(x['view']),*vals])
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','All variable spans','Half','Quarter'],rows)
body+='<p>At weight2, half-coverage detection is below1% in all eight cases. These are low-power failures under the fixed subset models, not evidence that localized effects are absent.</p>'
body+='<h2>Exact arithmetic checks before the power calculation</h2>'+table(['Check','Result'],[['Computation qualification',e(q['status'])],['Independent exact oracle checks',q['exact_oracle_checks']],['Tilt normalization vs binomial law','PASS'],['Asymmetric finite-law rejection regions','PASS'],['Enumerated product-distribution power','PASS'],['New observed-score tests / manuscript rescoring','NONE']])
body+='<p>Power uses exact integer/rational probability masses: no simulated detection counts, Monte Carlo confidence intervals or resampling precision issue. The selected and unaffected distributions recompose to each original null before tilting. Constant spans remain in the law.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>All312cases: null, forward/reverse, full/partial, low/high effects</summary>'+table(['Panel','Section','Reading','View','Coverage','Direction','Weight','Correct-direction power','Any rejection','Wrong direction','Mean shift D'],[[c['original_panel_index'],e(c['section']),c['reading'],e(c['view']),e(c['coverage']),c['direction'],e(c['weight_ratio']),pct(c['correct_direction_power']),pct(c['any_rejection']),pct(c['wrong_direction_rejection']),f'{c["mean_shift_D"]:.3f}'] for c in d['power_cases']])+'</details>'
body+='<h2>Interpretation and stop boundary</h2><p>The v96 nonrejections cannot exclude the frozen moderate effects, and strong effects can also be missed. Exact numerical resolution does not imply adequate power. The numerical solver, its toy qualification and the earlier adjacent-order finding are not invalidated by this audit.</p><p>No manuscript rescore was performed. All frozen benchmarks, partial/reverse alternatives and source-layout differences remain visible. A later revised test would require a separate frozen qualification; the family, effect sizes and thresholds were not relaxed here.</p><p>Results apply to this particular tilted conditional alternative family. Other mechanisms, heterogeneous effects, copying and stronger within-folio dependence may have different sensitivity. This is not a universal power statement about grammar or semantics.</p><p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen effects, coverage and gates</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Input/script hashes</a> · <a href="RESULTS.json">All exact power cases and span-selection ledgers</a> · <a href="COMPUTATION-QUALIFICATION.json">Arithmetic controls</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Independent checks</a> · <a href="../transition-control-v96/report.html">Unchanged v96</a></p><p>Browser appearance unreviewed; exact numerical verification is separate.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Actual-layout transition power · v97</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Actual-layout power report written; no manuscript rescore.')
